Fix a use-after-free in the parser for the experimental '=>' pipe-bind
syntax, so the parse target stops crashing on inputs that combine
'lhs |> var => expr' with anything that triggers a garbage collection
before the enclosing reduction.

xxpipe() in gram.y builds the call (function(var) expr)(lhs) for the
'=>' form and returns it without PRESERVE_SV, unlike every other reduce
action.  The value is then reachable only from the malloc'ed bison
value stack, which the collector does not scan, so any collection
before the enclosing rule reduces frees it.  The lexer itself can
trigger one: a literal such as .1L warns, and warning() evaluates the
R-level .signalSimpleWarning hook, whose argument matching allocates.
The next reduction (here the '=' chain after the pipe) hands the freed
cell to lang3()/PROTECT:

    ==14702==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free
    READ of size 8 ... in CHK memory.c:160
        #1 Rf_protect memory.c
        #2 Rf_list2 / Rf_lang3
        #4 xxbinary gram.c
        #5 Rf_yyparse gram.c
    freed by thread T0 here:
        #1 ReleasePage <- TryToReleasePages <- RunGenCollect <- R_gc_internal
        #5 CONS_NR <- Rf_matchArgs_NR <- ... <- vsignalWarning <- Rf_warning
        #21 NumericValue gram.c <- yylex <- Rf_yyparse

Preserve the value and release lhs/rhs as the fall-through path does
(gram.y and the checked-in gram.c), and add a gctorture regression test
to tests/reg-tests-1e.R.  Present since r80504 (R 4.2.0).

Found by fuzzing R with AFL++ + AddressSanitizer (ClusterFuzzLite parse
target, which enables _R_USE_PIPEBIND_; a crashing input in the stored
corpus stops the target at startup on every batch run).

Upstream status: reported as R Bugzilla bug 19162 with this fix
attached (also r-devel/r-svn PR #329).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

diff --git a/src/main/gram.c b/src/main/gram.c
index 25fb7e7a79..f405cff606 100644
--- a/src/main/gram.c
+++ b/src/main/gram.c
@@ -3588,7 +3588,12 @@ static SEXP xxpipe(SEXP lhs, SEXP rhs, YYLTYPE *lloc_rhs)
 	    SEXP alist = list1(R_MissingArg);
 	    SET_TAG(alist, var);
 	    SEXP fun = lang4(R_FunctionSymbol, alist, expr, R_NilValue);
-	    return lang2(fun, lhs);
+	    /* the result stays on the parser stack until the next
+	       reduction, so it must be preserved like any other value */
+	    PRESERVE_SV(ans = lang2(fun, lhs));
+	    RELEASE_SV(lhs);
+	    RELEASE_SV(rhs);
+	    return ans;
 	}
 
 	/* check for placeholder in the RHS function */
diff --git a/src/main/gram.y b/src/main/gram.y
index 8a7b7d4136..458bcd2a40 100644
--- a/src/main/gram.y
+++ b/src/main/gram.y
@@ -1279,7 +1279,12 @@ static SEXP xxpipe(SEXP lhs, SEXP rhs, YYLTYPE *lloc_rhs)
 	    SEXP alist = list1(R_MissingArg);
 	    SET_TAG(alist, var);
 	    SEXP fun = lang4(R_FunctionSymbol, alist, expr, R_NilValue);
-	    return lang2(fun, lhs);
+	    /* the result stays on the parser stack until the next
+	       reduction, so it must be preserved like any other value */
+	    PRESERVE_SV(ans = lang2(fun, lhs));
+	    RELEASE_SV(lhs);
+	    RELEASE_SV(rhs);
+	    return ans;
 	}
 
 	/* check for placeholder in the RHS function */
diff --git a/tests/reg-tests-1e.R b/tests/reg-tests-1e.R
index f6ab73955a..8282d167d7 100644
--- a/tests/reg-tests-1e.R
+++ b/tests/reg-tests-1e.R
@@ -3710,6 +3710,21 @@ stopifnot(identical(L00, ksmooth(x,y, x.points=NULL)),
 
 
 
+## parsing '<lhs> |> <var> => <expr>' left the reduced call unprotected on the
+## parser stack, so a GC before the enclosing reduction could free it
+## (found by fuzzing; '=>' is still opt-in, and stays enabled once seen)
+Sys.setenv("_R_USE_PIPEBIND_" = "true")
+gctorture(TRUE)
+e <- parse(text = "x |> b => f(b) + { y <- 1; y <- 1; y <- 1; y <- 1; y <- 1 }",
+           keep.source = FALSE)
+gctorture(FALSE)
+Sys.unsetenv("_R_USE_PIPEBIND_")
+ex <- quote((function(b) f(b))(x)); ex[[1]] <- ex[[1]][[2]] # no `(` call
+stopifnot(identical(e[[1]][[2]], ex))
+## gave garbage (or a crash) for the LHS of '+' in R <= 4.6.x
+
+
+
 ## keep at end
 rbind(last =  proc.time() - .pt,
       total = proc.time())
